            <title><![CDATA[Leonida – PC Recompilation of the Xbox Version of GTA 6 (101 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida</link>
            <guid>50595168</guid>
            <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:57:26 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida">https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50595168">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div data-hpc="true" containertiming="hpc"><article itemprop="text">
<p dir="auto"><h4 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Grand Theft Auto VI (Xbox Series) running natively on Windows, built on your PC from your own copy.
</h4><a id="user-content-grand-theft-auto-vi-xbox-series-running-natively-on-windows-built-on-your-pc-from-your-own-copy" aria-label="Permalink: Grand Theft Auto VI (Xbox Series) running natively on Windows, built on your PC from your own copy.
" href="#grand-theft-auto-vi-xbox-series-running-natively-on-windows-built-on-your-pc-from-your-own-copy"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">
  <a href="#project-status">Status</a> |
  <a href="#how-to-build">How to build</a> |
  <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a> |
  <a href="#want-to-help">Want to help?</a> |
  <a href="#credits">Credits</a> |
  <a href="#license">License</a> |
  <a href="https://discord.gg/rexed" rel="nofollow">Discord</a>
</p>
<p dir="auto">Leonida is a static recompilation project. The Xbox Series CPU is x86-64 like a PC, so the game's code is loaded
and run natively, and the console's system software is reimplemented. The console's precompiled RDNA2 GPU programs
are translated to SPIR-V for Vulkan. The game's models, textures and audio are read from your package. All of this
happens <strong>on your PC, from your own copy of the game</strong>.</p>
<div dir="auto"><p dir="auto">Important</p><p dir="auto">This repository <strong>does not contain the game, keys or an executable</strong>, and it does not explain how to get them. You
need your own copy, with its files already readable on disk. Nothing here decrypts or works around any protection.
Everything the build creates (the generated shaders, extracted assets, the runtime folder and your saves) comes
from your game and stays on your PC. Never share those files.</p>
</div>
<p dir="auto">Discord: <a href="https://discord.gg/rexed" rel="nofollow">https://discord.gg/rexed</a>
<br></p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Project status</h2><a id="user-content-project-status" aria-label="Permalink: Project status" href="#project-status"></a></p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Early. The game does not boot yet.</strong> Everything that can be done without the game's executable is in place, so
work on booting can start as soon as one is available to a developer.</p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>What</th>
<th>Status</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Finding and checking your copy (Xbox Series 1.0.2.1)</td>
<td>✅ Works</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shaders: carve, unpack native RDNA2 code, disassemble</td>
<td>✅ All 26,503</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shaders: RDNA2 → SPIR-V translation</td>
<td>✅ <strong>All 26,503</strong> (disassembled with LLVM 21; LLVM 23 leaves 1,471 rejected for now, #644): 2,236 VS, 12,101 PS, 2,689 CS, 9,282 mesh, 195 geometry. All pass <code>spirv-val</code>, with a per-shader metadata index for pipeline creation. <g-emoji alias="warning">⚠️</g-emoji> 21,545 are wave64: exact on 64-wide subgroups (AMD). On 32-wide subgroups (NVIDIA, Intel), compute and mesh shaders are exact with wave64 emulation (<code>--wave64-emulate</code>, on by default there); cross-half wave ops in vertex, pixel and geometry shaders are still approximate</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shader translator checked on a real GPU</td>
<td><g-emoji alias="warning">⚠️</g-emoji> The hand-written GPU tests (vertex fetch, texture sampling, exports, ALU ops, partial-register ops, barycentrics, wave-uniform branches, compute LDS/barriers/buffer stores, wave64 masks) have been run on more than 30 GPU and driver combinations, with results in <a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/issues/166" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/issues/166/hovercard">#166</a>: NVIDIA Turing, Ampere, Ada and Blackwell (Windows and Linux); AMD GCN3, RDNA1, RDNA2, RDNA3 and RDNA4 (Windows driver and RADV); Intel Gen9 (ANV); Apple M1 (MoltenVK, no geometry or mesh stages); and Mesa llvmpipe. Wave64 tests need 64-wide subgroups (AMD) or <code>LEONIDA_W64_EMULATE=1</code>. These are small test shaders: the game's own shaders are checked by <code>spirv-val</code> and by driver pipeline creation (<code>vk_pipeline_check</code>), not by their output</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Models (OBJ with real names, UVs, material references)</td>
<td>✅ Exported. Not all layouts are decoded yet</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Texture dictionaries and world texture pools (DDS)</td>
<td>✅ Exported. Pool entries stored as BCPack are still skipped by the export; a clean-room decoder (<code>tools/bcpack.py</code>) rebuilds BC1, BC3, BC4 and BC5, and is not wired into <code>rpf9dump</code> yet (<a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/blob/main/docs/textures.md">notes</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Audio banks (AWC: Opus, XMA2)</td>
<td>✅ Exported whole. Opus repackaged <strong>losslessly</strong> as Ogg Opus; PCM (codec 0/2) as WAV; XMA2 decoded with ffmpeg. <code>--wav</code> adds 16-bit PCM WAV (<a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/blob/main/docs/audio.md">notes</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Music/radio config</td>
<td>? Measured. <strong>1,589</strong> audio-config records with exact durations and AWC stream ids; station grouping and content-id lists; no per-track start offsets (<a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/blob/main/docs/audio_config.md">notes</a>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>PE loader and import shims</td>
<td><g-emoji alias="warning">⚠️</g-emoji> Runs a stand-in executable end to end (<code>gta6rt --run</code>: CRT startup, statics, heap, files, threads, GDK imports through the shims, exit code back). Untested against the real executable</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Xbox D3D12 → Vulkan</td>
<td><g-emoji alias="warning">⚠️</g-emoji> In progress. A Vulkan-backed device behind the Xbox-ABI proxy creates queues, command lists, fences, descriptor heaps, committed and reserved resources, render-target and depth views, texture views and samplers (which go into the bindless set), and query heaps. Barriers, clears, uploads, copies (BC included), colour resolves and occlusion, timestamp and pipeline-statistics queries run on Vulkan, checked on one GPU. No buffer views, root signatures, pipelines, draws or swapchain yet (<a href="https://github.com/ItsNotRexed/Leonida/blob/main/docs/d3d12_vulkan.md">plan</a>)</td>
</tr>
