<p dir="auto">At <strong>5.38 GB</strong>, <code>Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-5.4GB</code> outscores Unsloth's 9.14 GB <code>UD-Q2_K_XL</code> on both GSM8K and HumanEval at 41% smaller size (up from 76/200 and 24/164 untuned). At <strong>8.87 GB</strong>, <code>Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-8.9GB</code> matches the BF16 original on GSM8K and cuts KL <code>2.34×</code> on English/chat/code and <code>29.6%</code> across all 13 languages below <code>UD-Q2_K_XL</code>. Both run directly through <code>lamq</code> and <code>runtime_mlx</code> with custom Apple Silicon Metal kernels (including M5 <code>MetalPerformancePrimitives</code> MoE prefill + FlashAttention-2 SDPA + exact unbiased <code>temp &gt; 0</code> speculative sampling, plus opt-in dynamic sigmoid Top-K routing, tight-margin verify, and N-gram prompt lookup), optionally paired with the 178.9 MB <a href="https://huggingface.co/shinmegamiboson/Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-drafter" rel="nofollow">4-bit DSpark drafters</a>: on M5 Max, <strong>5.4 GB</strong> reaches <strong><code>1,807 tok/s</code></strong> <code>T=512</code> prefill (<code>1,047 tok/s</code> at <code>T=128</code>), <strong><code>75.3 tok/s</code></strong> serial decode, and <strong><code>124.4 tok/s</code></strong> median lossless drafted decode (<strong><code>142.9 tok/s</code></strong> math, <strong><code>126.5 tok/s</code></strong> reasoning, <strong><code>122.2 tok/s</code></strong> code, <strong><code>104.0 tok/s</code></strong> prose; up to <strong><code>~150–160 tok/s</code></strong> with opt-in <code>top6</code> / <code>max_logit_gap=0.30</code>; <code>5.98 GB</code> active RAM), and <strong>8.9 GB</strong> decodes at <strong><code>63.5 tok/s</code></strong> serial and <strong><code>106.0 tok/s</code></strong> median (<strong><code>125.8 tok/s</code></strong> reasoning, <strong><code>123.8 tok/s</code></strong> math; <code>9.41 GB</code> active RAM).</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Install and use the Apple Silicon runtime</h2><a id="user-content-install-and-use-the-apple-silicon-runtime" aria-label="Permalink: Install and use the Apple Silicon runtime" href="#install-and-use-the-apple-silicon-runtime"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">On Apple silicon, install the runtime package directly (this installs <code>mlx</code>, <code>mlx-lm</code>, <code>numpy</code>, and <code>huggingface-hub</code> without the PyTorch compiler dependencies):</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="pip install git+https://github.com/ShinMegamiBoson/lookatmyquant.git"><pre>pip install git+https://github.com/ShinMegamiBoson/lookatmyquant.git</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">From a local clone, <code>pip install -e .</code> installs the <code>lamq</code> command, or run <code>python -m runtime_mlx</code> without installing.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Command line.</strong> Pass either a local model folder or a Hugging Face repo ID:</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    -p &quot;What is 17 times 23? Show the steps.&quot;

lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter \
    -p &quot;Write a Python function that merges overlapping intervals.&quot; --stats

lamq chat shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter

lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-5.4GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-drafter \
    -p &quot;What is 17 times 23? Show the steps.&quot; --stats"><pre>lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    -p <span><span>"</span>What is 17 times 23? Show the steps.<span>"</span></span>

lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter \
    -p <span><span>"</span>Write a Python function that merges overlapping intervals.<span>"</span></span> --stats

lamq chat shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter

lamq generate shinmegamiboson/Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-5.4GB \
    --drafter shinmegamiboson/Inkling-2-Mini-LookAtMyQuant-drafter \
    -p <span><span>"</span>What is 17 times 23? Show the steps.<span>"</span></span> --stats</pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><code>lamq generate</code> reads stdin when <code>-p</code> is omitted, supports <code>--raw</code>, <code>--system</code>, <code>--thinking</code>, <code>--temp</code>, <code>--mode linear|chat-fork|copy-wide</code>, <code>--no-adaptive</code>, and <code>--json</code>. <code>lamq info &lt;model&gt;</code> inspects a packed model's format and dimensions without loading weights.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Python integration.</strong> <code>runtime_mlx.load</code> returns an <code>(model, tokenizer)</code> pair compatible with <code>mlx_lm.generate</code> and <code>mlx_lm.stream_generate</code> (auto-detecting <code>opgraph-packed-1</code> models such as Qwen3.5-4B / Qwen3.8-27B and <code>lamq.json</code> exports such as Gemma 4 E2B):</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="from mlx_lm import generate
from runtime_mlx import load

model, tok = load(&quot;shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB&quot;)
prompt = tok.apply_chat_template(
    [{&quot;role&quot;: &quot;user&quot;, &quot;content&quot;: &quot;What is 17 times 23? Show the steps.&quot;}],
    add_generation_prompt=True,
    enable_thinking=False,
)
print(generate(model, tok, prompt, max_tokens=200))"><pre><span>from</span> <span>mlx_lm</span> <span>import</span> <span>generate</span>
<span>from</span> <span>runtime_mlx</span> <span>import</span> <span>load</span>

<span>model</span>, <span>tok</span> <span>=</span> <span>load</span>(<span>"shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB"</span>)
<span>prompt</span> <span>=</span> <span>tok</span>.<span>apply_chat_template</span>(
    [{<span>"role"</span>: <span>"user"</span>, <span>"content"</span>: <span>"What is 17 times 23? Show the steps."</span>}],
    <span>add_generation_prompt</span><span>=</span><span>True</span>,
    <span>enable_thinking</span><span>=</span><span>False</span>,
)
<span>print</span>(<span>generate</span>(<span>model</span>, <span>tok</span>, <span>prompt</span>, <span>max_tokens</span><span>=</span><span>200</span>))</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">For streaming, multi-turn chat, or speculative decoding through one interface, use <code>Runtime</code>:</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="from runtime_mlx import Runtime

rt = Runtime.load(
    &quot;shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB&quot;,
    drafter=&quot;shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter&quot;,
)
for chunk in rt.stream(&quot;Solve 3x + 4y = 31 and 5x - 2y = 17.&quot;, max_tokens=256):
    print(chunk.text, end=&quot;&quot;, flush=True)"><pre><span>from</span> <span>runtime_mlx</span> <span>import</span> <span>Runtime</span>

<span>rt</span> <span>=</span> <span>Runtime</span>.<span>load</span>(
    <span>"shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB"</span>,
    <span>drafter</span><span>=</span><span>"shinmegamiboson/Qwen3.8-27B-LookAtMyQuant-7.2GB-drafter"</span>,
)
<span>for</span> <span>chunk</span> <span>in</span> <span>rt</span>.<span>stream</span>(<span>"Solve 3x + 4y = 31 and 5x - 2y = 17."</span>, <span>max_tokens</span><span>=</span><span>256</span>):
    <span>print</span>(<span>chunk</span>.<span>text</span>, <span>end</span><span>=</span><span>""</span>, <span>flush</span><span>=</span><span>True</span>)</pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Run the compiler on SmolLM2-360M in three commands</h2><a id="user-content-run-the-compiler-on-smollm2-360m-in-three-commands" aria-label="Permalink: Run the compiler on SmolLM2-360M in three commands" href="#run-the-compiler-on-smollm2-360m-in-three-commands"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">Install the dependencies and download the model and WikiText-2. The code reads SmolLM2-360M's config when it starts, so do this first.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="pip install -r requirements.txt
python -c &quot;from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download as d; d('HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M')&quot;
python -c &quot;from datasets import load_dataset as l; l('Salesforce/wikitext', 'wikitext-2-raw-v1')&quot;"><pre>pip install -r requirements.txt
python -c <span><span>"</span>from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download as d; d('HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M')<span>"</span></span>
python -c <span><span>"</span>from datasets import load_dataset as l; l('Salesforce/wikitext', 'wikitext-2-raw-v1')<span>"</span></span></pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Measure.</strong> This compresses one piece at a time, leaves the rest exact, and records the KL to the original model. The full set for this model, 2,312 measurements, took about 50 minutes on an L40S.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="python compiler.py measure --model HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M --part linear --layers 0-3 --out results/batch/my_measurements.json"><pre>python compiler.py measure --model HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M --part linear --layers 0-3 --out results/batch/my_measurements.json</pre></div>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Allocate.</strong> This picks one code per piece, with the least summed KL inside the budget. It needs no GPU. This command uses the SmolLM2-360M measurements in this repository, with a budget of 3.044 bits per weight.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="python compiler.py allocate --sens 'results/batch/ccSens*.json' --target disk --items linear --bits 3.044 --out results/compiler/plans/my_plan.json"><pre>python compiler.py allocate --sens <span><span>'</span>results/batch/ccSens*.json<span>'</span></span> --target disk --items linear --bits 3.044 --out results/compiler/plans/my_plan.json</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The plan it writes has the same widths as <code>results/compiler/plans/sm_lin_3044.json</code>.</p>
<p dir="auto"><strong>Build and score.</strong> This quantizes the model to the plan, one matrix at a time. It then reports perplexity and KL to the original on WikiText-2 test.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="python quantize.py --program plan --model HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M --plan results/compiler/plans/my_plan.json --out results/my_run.json"><pre>python quantize.py --program plan --model HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM2-360M --plan results/compiler/plans/my_plan.json --out results/my_run.json</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Our run of that plan is in <code>results/batch/cc_sm_lin_3044.json</code>. It reached perplexity 16.64 and KL 0.0926, against an original perplexity of 15.31. Add <code>--layers 1 --calib 8 --eval 2</code> for a quick check that everything works.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">Run the LookAtMyQuant 2 recipe on Qwen3.5-4B</h2><a id="user-content-run-the-lookatmyquant-2-recipe-on-qwen35-4b" aria-label="Permalink: Run the LookAtMyQuant 2 recipe on Qwen3.5-4B" href="#run-the-lookatmyquant-2-recipe-on-qwen35-4b"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">Each step is a named job; <code>python run_batch.py --list</code> prints its command. The jobs need Qwen3.5-4B in <code>models/Qwen3.5-4B</code> on the volume and the text mix (<code>modal run --detach modal_fetch.py --text</code>). Every file they make goes to <code>lm2/</code> on the volume.</p>
<div dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Text
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Calibration,lm2Solutions
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2RowImportance
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Build
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Finetune
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Math,lm2Math216,lm2TextKL"><pre>modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Text
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Calibration,lm2Solutions
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2RowImportance
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Build
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Finetune
modal run --detach modal_app.py --jobs lm2Math,lm2Math216,lm2TextKL</pre></div>
