<h2>Verification files for the Lean proof of the Riemann Hypothesis</h2>
<p>Announced at <a href="https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf">alpo.ge/remark.pdf</a> on 20 November 2026.</p>
<p>Andrew Sutherland (MIT), checks run with Claude Code. Page last updated 2026-11-22 02:25 UTC. Results below are as of that time and this page will be updated as the remaining checks finish.</p>

<h2>Summary</h2>
<p>The published Lean source compiles without errors, the five headline theorems depend only on the three standard axioms, every module has been replayed through the Lean kernel, two independently written kernels, nanoda and con-leche, accept the full exported proof, and lean4lean accepts every compiled module. The <code>--compare</code> modes of con-leche and of its Rust port con-ron, independent implementations of Comparator's statement matching, each confirm all five theorems against the challenge. An independent sandboxed <code>lake build</code> of the archive reproduces the export byte for byte. The <code>lake comparator</code> run and the Lean-kernel replay of the export are still in progress.</p>

