<h2>Check it yourself</h2>
<p>With Lean v4.36.0 installed, nothing needs to be built. You need roughly 100 GB of RAM and 70 GB of disk.</p>
<pre>zstd -d --long=30 solution.ndjson.zst      # --long=30 is required
zstd -d --long=27 challenge.ndjson.zst
sha256sum solution.ndjson challenge.ndjson  # compare with the hashes above

lake comparator --config comparator.json \
  --challenge-from-export challenge.ndjson --solution-from-export solution.ndjson</pre>
<p>nanoda alone took about 28 minutes on 80 threads. The Lean kernels are single-threaded and take much longer.</p>
<p>The fastest independent check is con-leche built from source (Lean v4.36.0, about two minutes to build). It needs about 50 GB of RAM and took under four minutes on 64 threads:</p>
<pre>git clone https://github.com/leanprover/con-leche &amp;&amp; cd con-leche
git checkout compare        # 5dc36dc1; master (cd2eceab) for the plain check
lake build con-leche
.lake/build/bin/con-leche --compare challenge.ndjson solution.ndjson</pre>

