<table>
<tbody><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Source archive</td><td><code>lean.tar.gz</code>, the 14 parts from alpo.ge joined; 239,275,554 bytes<br><span>sha256 9631b4f020199e580ba86178cb56c6e9b09f690c2369a80dc4334aa93f49c7fc</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Source mirror</td><td><a href="https://github.com/Deicyde/riemann-hypothesis">Deicyde/riemann-hypothesis</a>, byte-identical to the archive apart from the Comparator files it adds</td></tr>
<tr><td>Lean / Mathlib</td><td>Lean v4.33.1 (commit <code>819816b2</code>); Mathlib tag <code>v4.33.1</code> (<code>0df444a3</code>)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Exporter</td><td>lean4export tag <code>v4.33.0</code> (<code>15f6055e</code>), built with Lean v4.33.1; target list as in Deicyde's <code>export-targets.txt</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Judge and extra kernels</td><td>Lean v4.36.0: <code>lake comparator</code>, <code>leanchecker</code>, <code>leanchecker-paranoid</code>, <code>nanoda_bin</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>lean4lean</td><td><a href="https://github.com/digama0/lean4lean">digama0/lean4lean</a> at <code>67f63b0c</code>, built with Lean v4.33.1; run on the compiled <code>.olean</code> files, not the export</td></tr>
<tr><td>con-leche</td><td><a href="https://github.com/leanprover/con-leche">leanprover/con-leche</a> <code>master</code> at <code>cd2eceab</code> and branch <code>compare</code> at <code>5dc36dc1</code>, each built with Lean v4.36.0</td></tr>
<tr><td>con-ron</td><td><a href="https://github.com/leanprover/con-ron">leanprover/con-ron</a> <code>master</code> at <code>3f22699b</code>, the Rust port of con-leche, built with <code>cargo build --release</code></td></tr>
<tr><td><code>Main.olean</code></td><td><span>sha256 9146dfb4148e24d2252e04c50742f3e49dd126dfcc5006d10bf5f873ddf796ad</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>Manifest of all compiled files</td><td><span>sha256 375cbee2fc3fc0f5088ef2e6dc9a5ac5530924310dc62422ec65aac9dc4c1d25</span><br>specific to the build directory <code>/home/ubuntu/grh/src/lean</code>, and one file in it is not deterministic; see <a href="#manifest-path">the note below</a></td></tr>
<tr><td>Build directory</td><td>the archive's <code>lean/</code> directory was at <code>/home/ubuntu/grh/src/lean</code> on every build machine, so each source file was passed to Lean as <code>/home/ubuntu/grh/src/lean/src/&lt;Module/Path&gt;.lean</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>

<h2>Caveats</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>How the original build was done, and the rebuild that checks it.</strong> The original build ran on cloud machines without a sandbox, and compiled each file by calling <code>lean</code> directly with the same inputs <code>lake</code> supplies (module name, package name and the lakefile's options), not through <code>lake build</code>. All the kernel checks above were run on the export from that build. We then repeated the build on a separate machine with <code>lake build Main</code> inside a bubblewrap sandbox: no network, the source tree read-only, only <code>.lake</code> writable, the archive downloaded afresh from the author's site, and Mathlib's files checked against the official cache first. The export made inside that sandbox is byte-identical to the published one, so every check on the published export applies to it.</li>
  <li id="manifest-path"><strong>The per-file <code>.olean</code> hashes depend on the build directory, and one module is not deterministic.</strong> In Lean v4.33.1 a compiled file stores each linter message together with the absolute path of its source file. Of our 175,187 compiled files, 98,219 contain the path <code>/home/ubuntu/grh/src/lean/src/…</code>; the other 76,968, including <code>Main.olean</code>, contain no path. So <code>project-oleans.sha256</code> can be reproduced only by a build whose source tree is at <code>/home/ubuntu/grh/src/lean</code>; elsewhere, only the files of modules that emit no linter messages should match.<br>
  The sandboxed <code>lake build</code> was run at that same path, and 175,186 of its 175,187 files are byte-identical to our manifest. The exception is <code>Formalism/LocalToGlobal/SiegelLatticeTheory/CokernelGLCounts/RankPointCounts/LocModel.olean</code>: same size, different contents. Recompiling that one module six times on one machine with identical inputs gave one output four times and the other twice, and those are exactly the two hashes in the two manifests. We have not investigated what differs inside the file. Because of it, the sha256 of the whole manifest file is not reproducible even at the same path; compare file by file.</li>
  <li>A passing check shows that the formal statements, as written in Lean against Mathlib's definitions, follow from the three standard axioms according to the kernels used. It relies on those kernels and on Mathlib's definitions being what they are intended to be.</li>
</ul>

</div></div>]]></description>
