            <title><![CDATA[FBI reportedly investigating apparent hack of its criminal database (177 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvze7de86pk3o</link>
            <guid>50587859</guid>
            <pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:33:57 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvze7de86pk3o">https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvze7de86pk3o</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50587859">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div id="bbc-main"><article><div data-component="image-block"><figure><div><p><img src="https://static.files.bbci.co.uk/bbcdotcom/web/20261119-102257-f8058bdc4a-3.28.2-1/grey-placeholder.png" aria-label="image unavailable"><img sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 50vw, (min-width: 1008px) 66vw, 96vw" srcset="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/240/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 240w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/320/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 320w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 480w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/640/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 640w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/800/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 800w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1024/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 1024w,https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/1536/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp 1536w" src="https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/news/480/cpsprodpb/b03e/live/13380570-e557-11f1-ad51-c3505e495cd9.jpg.webp" loading="eager" alt="Getty Images The front of the FBI building in DC. The concrete structure shows a minimal FBI Bureau sign and flies two American flags on either side of the doorway. "><span>Getty Images</span></p></div></figure></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>The FBI is investigating an apparent breach of its criminal information database, US media reports, citing two people briefed on the issue.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>The National Crime Information Center (NCIC) database is used by federal and local law enforcement to share information on warrants and background checks. </p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>It would not be the first time hackers have targeted the FBI, the domestic intelligence and security service of the US. The agency did not immediately respond to the BBC's request for comment.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>When asked about the breach on Saturday in a Fox News interview, President Donald Trump said he had "just heard" about the hack. "I will say that it's not good. I don't like that," he said.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>"But maybe we'll learn things that we would've never learned otherwise," the president added.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>This apparent breach of FBI database comes after a string of tech outages which hit banking, air traffic control and other sectors in the US last week. Officials have said they were not caused by cyberattacks, but the blackouts have sparked scrutiny from lawmakers.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>After that hack, one former FBI agent told the BBC he feared for the safety of current employees, whose personal information could soon become available online to criminals and hostile nation-state hackers.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>In a separate development, NBC reported an apparent cyberattack against the US Department of Agriculture (USDA) . </p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>Employees were informed on Thursday that its farm payment system had been targeted, NBC said.</p></div><div data-component="text-block"><p>The USDA has not publicly commented on the issue.</p></div></article></div></div>]]></description>
        </item>
